.TH S3AR-LIST 1 "September 2026" "S3 Archiver" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
s3ar-list \- list live S3 buckets and objects
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B s3ar-list
.RB [ \-v ]
.I s3://[BUCKET[/KEY]]...
.br
.B s3ar-list
.B \-b
.RB [ \-v ]
.B s3://
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B s3ar-list
lists live S3 objects selected by one or more S3 URIs. The URI
.B s3://
selects all buckets and their objects. A bucket URI selects that bucket and
its objects; a key URI selects the exact key and keys below that prefix.
.PP
With
.BR \-b ,
list bucket names only. This mode requires exactly
.BR s3:// .
.PP
Listing results are written to standard output; diagnostics go to standard
error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-b , " " \-\-buckets
List buckets only.
.TP
.BR \-v , " " \-\-verbose
Include object size, modification time and ETag, or bucket ACL information.
The option may be repeated to increase diagnostic verbosity.
.TP
.BR \-h , " " \-\-help
Show usage on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR s3ar (1),
.BR s3ar-get (1),
.BR s3ar-put (1)
